# Debugging & Development Patterns

## 🐛 Debugging Approach Used
All debug statements in [Core.lua](mdc:Core/Core.lua) and modules are **commented out** to prevent chat activation issues that could interfere with Explorer Mode.

```lua
-- Example pattern used throughout codebase:
function AzeriteMOP:Debug(...)
    -- if self.DEBUG then
    --     print("|cFF4488FF[AzeriteMOP]|r", ...)
    -- end
end

-- Usage in functions:
-- self:Debug("Database initialized successfully!")
```

## ✅ Safe Debugging Methods
- Use `/reload` for testing changes
- Leverage slash commands for runtime testing (`/az testexplorer`, `/az checkframes`)
- Frame inspection: Check `frame:IsShown()`, `frame:GetFrameLevel()`
- Manual triggering of module functions for testing

## 🎯 Error Handling Patterns
```lua
-- Safe frame access
if self.PlayerFrame and self.PlayerFrame.frame then
    self.PlayerFrame.frame:Show()
else
    print("PlayerFrame not found")
end

-- Compatibility checks
if not AzeriteMOP:IsMoPClassic() then
    error("This addon requires MoP Classic!")
end
```

## 📋 Testing Checklist
- Test with `/reload` after changes
- Verify Explorer Mode activation/deactivation
- Check chat frame visibility and functionality  
- Test magnification effect with scroll wheel
- Validate whisper suggestions appear correctly
